The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This isolated route inherits the original CED/mapper/data/staging definitions,
and uses eight GPUs, microbatch4, accumulation4. It adds explicit raw HRM text
inheritance, fixed BP5, PrefixLM attention, role-specific LR floors and named
full-state restore validation. The existing source implementations are unchanged.
Task-start source identities are recorded in source_guard.json.

The HRM recurrence and attention gate derive from sapientinc/HRM-Text;
see ../../text_hrm_h2l3/NOTICE and LICENSE.HRM-Text for Apache-2.0 provenance.
This route imports the project's trained SmolLM2 HRM implementation, including
its MagicNorm adaptation, without converting or reinitializing trained weights.
